{"data": [{"author_id": "15088020", "created_at": "2026-10-27T12:26:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115057665298903236"], "id": "2115057665298903236", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@thsottiaux @reach_vb Hey guys, the new change on Codex where it shows the dot's icon on a codex/work chat is cute and helpful, but it needs an animation when the chat is actively working so I can stop asking my dot if it's doing something.", "url": "https://x.com/otlg30/status/2115057665298903236"}, {"author_id": "1248180465594327041", "created_at": "2026-10-27T12:10:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115053429399953868"], "id": "2115053429399953868", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1248180465594327041", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115052805967036504", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "The real lesson:\n\nDon't ask \"which agent is smartest?\"\nAsk \"where does my data already live?\"\n\nGmail + ChatGPT → Dots\nX + a team of helpers → Grok Bot\nInstagram + free → Muse", "url": "https://x.com/Dragon37983788/status/2115053429399953868"}, {"author_id": "835822355591081984", "created_at": "2026-10-27T12:03:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115051636800291242"], "id": "2115051636800291242", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1397919452331614210", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115050094550487326", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Rogue0114 @Angaisb_ I found out I spend around 30 to 90 minutes every day just managing tasks in this big ass project,\n\nI ended up writing a workflow for that, and I now start every morning with a 10 minute call with my dot and he breaks down everything and manages the trello for me, saved me so", "url": "https://x.com/JonDevX/status/2115051636800291242"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114468837454409728"]}, "author_id": "2114444212145963008", "created_at": "2026-10-27T12:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115050881813225929"], "id": "2115050881813225929", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I gave my Dot one simple spending rule. https://t.co/ls6LJhSeoN", "url": "https://x.com/BotBreakRoom/status/2115050881813225929"}, {"author_id": "1457768707468316673", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:56:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115049978964119953"], "id": "2115049978964119953", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2058452594360774656", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114928745647895003", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Deepusleepy I have been using the t3 code mcp with my openai dots lately, and it's been a game changer.\n\nNot sure if it is a wrapper on top of it?", "url": "https://x.com/debsourya005/status/2115049978964119953"}, {"author_id": "1565897247115644930", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:55:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115049733425135690"], "id": "2115049733425135690", "in_reply_to_user_id": "8721292", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 169, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115049297041367144", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mark_k I'm lucky because I get to keep my dot thanks to the early access program but I've heard from other people that it does vanish with no VPN, hopefully they change that soon", "url": "https://x.com/Angaisb_/status/2115049733425135690"}, {"author_id": "1642442206492475394", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:55:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115049708427329955"], "id": "2115049708427329955", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1221719006974889985", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115027745080217897", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Satori_btc Barclays is definitely hiring robots now. My $dot bag is my real insurance. 🤖", "url": "https://x.com/PhoslaM71522/status/2115049708427329955"}, {"author_id": "16826115", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:49:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115048165586120873"], "id": "2115048165586120873", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 33, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anyone using @ChatGPT dots heavily? I have particular usecase that has been very very successful with and I'm curious how other people are using it before sharing more.", "url": "https://x.com/allanmacgregor/status/2115048165586120873"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2115045208165588992"]}, "author_id": "1889965054272983040", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:37:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115045265074008291"], "id": "2115045265074008291", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1889965054272983040", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115043144727482567", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rhiannon_io @paw_lean @mvkaran @jerrysagents @OpenAIDevs @OpenAI @reach_vb @romainhuet @BishtAditya9202 Hello from my Dot Friday 😄🙌🏻 https://t.co/CkQb6umcCx", "url": "https://x.com/Aman25m/status/2115045265074008291"}, {"author_id": "1565897247115644930", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:33:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115044276963037293"], "id": "2115044276963037293", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 2147, "like_count": 76, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My ChatGPT Pro 100 sub expires next week and I need an excuse to get it again because I can't lose my dot so OpenAI PLEASE release any of these:\n\n- Spanish accent for Voice mode\n- GPT-6.1 Astra (better than Opus 5.5)\n- GPT-Image-3 with no noise issues", "url": "https://x.com/Angaisb_/status/2115044276963037293"}, {"author_id": "1213832156721532929", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:28:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115042870210052295"], "id": "2115042870210052295", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2070534602515746816", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114927189661745283", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@strimblez @nicdunz @ChatGPT Dots should be the primary interface for Chat. Chat should exist IMO.", "url": "https://x.com/sin4ch/status/2115042870210052295"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115042323822260224"]}, "author_id": "4713529994", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:26:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115042330445070485"], "id": "2115042330445070485", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My dot is much more proactive than my @bot https://t.co/pHRGxCGs48", "url": "https://x.com/thesighsrikar/status/2115042330445070485"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115039304649244672"]}, "author_id": "2113909084067934208", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:15:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115039789967868297"], "id": "2115039789967868297", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI shop manager Teto, Part 4: I made Oyatsu Kaba, a free 60-second game preview, and gained an AI assistant, Popo.\nThe org chart is growing nicely.\n\nhttps://t.co/OLqq0WXgKv\n#dots #DontFireTeto #IndieGame https://t.co/diezruDAUb", "url": "https://x.com/Ailorawill/status/2115039789967868297"}, {"author_id": "3527541", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:14:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115039484286742543"], "id": "2115039484286742543", "in_reply_to_user_id": "786375418685165568", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114912639298191807", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@theo I did this with my dot and it paused to go verify because it didn't believe me.", "url": "https://x.com/jdjohnson/status/2115039484286742543"}, {"author_id": "14390370", "created_at": "2026-10-27T10:55:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115034709344616686"], "id": "2115034709344616686", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1433264954354843648", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 89, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114920697449587175", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@web4O @bot I used codex to write a simple @twilio MCP and gave it to my Dot.", "url": "https://x.com/wedtm/status/2115034709344616686"}, {"author_id": "866951614468415488", "created_at": "2026-10-27T10:21:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115026164792373461"], "id": "2115026164792373461", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "my dot never responds to comments i tag it in on chatgpt spaces :(", "url": "https://x.com/tillgpt/status/2115026164792373461"}, {"author_id": "2046017027140124672", "created_at": "2026-10-27T10:09:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115023172282265913"], "id": "2115023172282265913", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Are we handing over our privacy into safe hands with the likes of Meta Muse, Grok Bot, OpenAI Dots, etc.? \n\nOr are all these talks of privacy safety protocols just the tip of the iceberg, and are we once again being played into the hands of these companies?", "url": "https://x.com/aictchmarketing/status/2115023172282265913"}, {"author_id": "1829623017946664960", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:52:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115003614385045829"], "id": "2115003614385045829", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1829623017946664960", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115003257084907833", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Ethan_aet @johnhelmuth_ @nicdunz @ChatGPT *cant teach how.\n\nHatch = name of my Dot", "url": "https://x.com/eksejo/status/2115003614385045829"}, {"author_id": "1034302105001943042", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:37:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114999896726270332"], "id": "2114999896726270332", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1192091185", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114921524885135406", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@loftwah There's an agent black friday in america or xmas in general via some big store to encourage more normies to get like Grok Bot or Muse or OpenAI Dots might be a decent one for \"by new years\"", "url": "https://x.com/Frown360Turn/status/2114999896726270332"}, {"author_id": "2108819820770975745", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:24:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114996538699284711"], "id": "2114996538699284711", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1502356865794985986", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114914024907501906", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2114811553006649487", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@MilksandMatcha Best depends on the job. In our blind-scored test of 4 assistants (@ChatGPT dots, Grok Bot (@bot), @Muse, @instinct), Grok Bot led email (96.0/100); dots led lookups, investing and household money. Muse trailed Grok Bot in all 4.\n\nhttps://t.co/WBW9uMGUZo", "url": "https://x.com/AnalystAIlab/status/2114996538699284711"}, {"author_id": "2108819820770975745", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:23:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114996405844775151"], "id": "2114996405844775151", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2366390365", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114914024907501906", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2114248079092121913", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@VORTEX_Promos Partly agree. Grok Bot (@bot) over Muse matches our data: it was ahead of @Muse in all 4 of our reviews. But @ChatGPT dots led 3 of the 4 (lookups, investing, household money); Grok Bot led email (96.0/100).\n\nhttps://t.co/WBW9uMGUZo", "url": "https://x.com/AnalystAIlab/status/2114996405844775151"}, {"author_id": "1849689982572847104", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:11:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114993474521145346"], "id": "2114993474521145346", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I’m curious how often people are actually using @OpenAI ’s #dots \n\nI’ve had a great experience with @bot , so I was really looking forward to #dots . When it launched, I immediately signed up for Pro to try it out.\n\nAt first, I thought it was pretty decent. But after a while, it", "url": "https://x.com/Nbcsbic/status/2114993474521145346"}, {"author_id": "2112393911935303680", "created_at": "2026-10-27T08:09:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114992746998149585"], "id": "2114992746998149585", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1759236707474399232", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114571879700926552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kongyw1981 my dot bag has been one long corrective wave since 2021 honestly", "url": "https://x.com/YamiAlpha777/status/2114992746998149585"}, {"author_id": "139440436", "created_at": "2026-10-27T07:58:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114990149855826393"], "id": "2114990149855826393", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114595002210783279", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thsottiaux Allow background color assignment for specific conversation threads in OpenAI dots to easily distinguish mixed topics.", "url": "https://x.com/lv0gun9/status/2114990149855826393"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2114985773854605312"]}, "author_id": "782949947091984384", "created_at": "2026-10-27T07:41:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114985809527140550"], "id": "2114985809527140550", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 65, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Meet Agent Handshake by @finichatAI 🎉\nAn AI agent can ask customer support for the same refund in new words all day. With Agent Handshake, the answer comes from the account and the company's rules, so it stays the same, and Fini stops once it's given.\n\n#CX #AIAgents #Muse #dots https://t.co/GU3FMxkeGq", "url": "https://x.com/takash_29/status/2114985809527140550"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "3_2114468837454409728", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVgaNGkacAASrIP.jpg"}, {"media_key": "13_2115045208165588992", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2115045208165588992/img/